@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081
@customerId = 2

### 1. Crear un cliente (debe responder 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana Pérez",
  "email": "ana@mail.com",
  "phone": "0991234567",
  "address": "Av. Amazonas N24-12, Quito"
}

### 2. Listar clientes
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers

### 3. Consultar el cliente 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{customerId}}

### 4. Actualizar el cliente 1
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{customerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana Pérez López",
  "email": "ana@mail.com",
  "phone": "0991234567",
  "address": "Av. 6 de Diciembre N30-15, Quito"
}

### 5. Cliente que no existe (debe responder 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/999

### 6. Datos inválidos (debe responder 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "email": "esto-no-es-un-email",
  "address": "Quito"
}

### 7. Email repetido (debe responder 409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Otra Ana",
  "email": "ana@mail.com",
  "address": "Quito"
}

### 8. Eliminar el cliente 1 (debe responder 204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{customerId}}